# XSH sched_getscheduler()
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#
# A negative pid is unspecified and not tested. Which processes the caller
# may query is implementation-defined: the EPERM case cannot be provoked
# portably, so the other-process test runs privileged and treats a refusal
# as UNRESOLVED.

assertion  XSH.sched_getscheduler.001
anchor     functions/sched_getscheduler.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/sched_getscheduler.html#RETURN VALUE
class      conditional
when       PS
since      2001
says       sched_getscheduler(0) returns a non-negative policy, and
           sched_getscheduler(getpid()) returns the same one.
test       t/001-self.c

assertion  XSH.sched_getscheduler.002
anchor     functions/sched_getscheduler.html#ERRORS/ESRCH
anchor     functions/sched_getscheduler.html#RETURN VALUE
class      conditional
when       PS
since      2001
says       For the pid of a child that has been reaped, sched_getscheduler()
           returns -1 with ESRCH.
test       t/002-esrch.c

assertion  XSH.sched_getscheduler.003
anchor     functions/sched_getscheduler.html#DESCRIPTION
class      conditional
when       PS
since      2001
says       sched_getscheduler(pid) of another existing process returns the
           policy of that process (SCHED_FIFO for a child that set it), not
           the caller's.
needs      root
timeout    60
test       t/003-other-process.c
